@startuml
!include _style.iuml
title Trust view · protected routes · 76282d3
left to right direction
skinparam defaultFontSize 22
skinparam ArrowFontSize 20
skinparam LegendFontSize 18
skinparam titleFontSize 23
skinparam BackgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 28
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
component "frontend/\npublisher/" as client <<untrusted>> $CLIENT
component "HttpApi\nGatewayAuthorizer\nREQUEST\nCookie · TTL 0" as gateway $INFRA
' https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/contracts/gateway.py#L3-L5
' https://github.com/Collaboration95/dc2/blob/76282d3/scripts/aws/v1/definitions.py#L1546-L1621
package "Backend invocation boundary" as backend <<trust boundary>> $INFRA {
 package "Media identity authority" as authority $MEDIA {
  component "MediaAuthorizer\nHS256\nsub / exp / iat" as auth
  database "media_db\nusers" as users
  auth ..> users : current User
 }
 component "MediaApi\n----\nGatewayAdapter\ncurrent_user(): cookie + User\ncompare Actor" as media $MEDIA
 component "ProcessingApi\n----\nGatewayAdapter\ngateway_actor(): Actor" as processing $PROC
 media ..> users : recheck User
}
client ..> gateway : access_token\ncookie
 gateway ..> auth : CUSTOM\nroutes
 auth ..> gateway : <<flow>>\nboolean + Actor
 gateway ..> media : AWS_PROXY\ncookie + Actor
 gateway ..> processing : AWS_PROXY\ncookie + Actor
legend bottom
 Blue = Media; amber = Processing; green = client; slate = infrastructure.
 Dashed = required dependency; <<flow>> returns authorization context. Boundary is not a subnet.
 Lambda resource policies restrict Gateway invocation. The Actor marker is a schema fence, not a secret.
 Each API runs GatewayAdapter: strips x-owner-id / x-role, validates / injects Actor, preserves cookies.
 Health and register/login/logout are public exceptions. Operator/readiness invokes use separate IAM authority.
endlegend
@enduml
